      "title": "Photography Direction",
      "content": "The visual identity is inseparable from the photography. All editorial imagery should be shot in low-key, high-contrast conditions — night or interior, single source light, deep shadow. Subjects are models in YSL product (leather, denim, tailored black), photographed in tight to medium framing with direct, unsmiling gaze. Color in the photograph should be muted toward black, charcoal, oxblood, ivory — never saturated primary colors. Avoid studio white, lifestyle warmth, candid documentary, or bright daylight. The mood reference is a Helmut Newton still or a Hedi Slimane campaign: noir, intimate, uncompromising."
    }
  ],
